  "query_preview": "..\n/Issued 250 PM MDT Tue Sep 1 2026/ \n\nSouthwesterly flow on the west side of a quick moving upper level\nridge has begun to bring increasing moisture and warmth to \nSouthwestern and North Central Montana. Most lower elevations \nlocales have reached the upper 70s/low 80s, which is just slightly\nwarmer than our average highs for this time of year. In addition \nto the warmth, a few showers and thunderstorms have begun to pop \nup across Beaverhead County, and these will gradually drift to the\nnorth/northeast through the remainder of the evening. While \nsevere wind gusts are not expected, a few gusts to around 50 mph \nwill be possible with some of the stronger storms. \n\nWinds increase on Wednesday as a shortwave trough embedded in the\nflow moves overhead. Winds will be strongest across Southwestern \nMontana, particularly during the late morning and afternoon, \nespecially in the north/south oriented valleys. As this shortwave \nprogresses further north, showers and thunderstorms will develop \nand move northward towards the plains. As these storms reach the \nplains, the combination of strong winds aloft, along with dry mid \nlevels and a very deep and well mixed boundary layer, some of the \nstorms will begin to produce strong wind gusts, some of which will\nlikely be over 60 mph. With this in mind, SPC has upgraded our \nMarginal risk to a Slight risk (1/5 to 2/5) for tomorrow \nafternoon.\n\nWinds will continue across Southwestern Montana as an upper level\njet streak moves overhead, but winds are likely not going to be\nquite as strong as Wednesday. Thursday should also bring generally\ndrier conditions to the Treasure State East of the Divide, aside\nfrom a few isolated stray showers. Looking ahead to the weekend,\nan upper level low situated just off the coast of Oregon and\nWashington will keep us on the unsettled side, and may eventually\nallow some moisture from what is currently Tropical Storm Marie to\nwork its way through the Western US and into Montana early next\nweek. Ludwig",
